==Battleground==
*2 [[Wall Doge]]s spawn, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*4 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*2 [[Maawth]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 133.33~136.67 seconds<sup>4,000f~4,100f</sup>.
*3 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[THE FOLIVOREAN]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Wild Doge]]s spawn, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
**5 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn, delay 36.67~40 seconds<sup>1,100f~1,200f</sup>.
**1 [[Infernal Pegasus Deonil]] spawns after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
**2 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 73.33 seconds<sup>2,200f</sup>, delay 73.33~76.67 seconds<sup>2,200f~2,300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
A somewhat simple stage that marks the first usage of Infernal Pegasus Deonil outside of empress' excavation.
The main idea is to chip down Deonil with Courier while bursting down the peons with cats specifically prepared to take them out. The FOLIVOREAN will die to your spam over time.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: Despite the attempts of the devs to counter it, Courier is still the best and most easily accessible option to take down Deonil. With the combination of its Massive Damage and Beheoth Slayer abilities, it deals 10x more damage to Deonil, meaning around 110,000 damage per shot at level 30.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: Can Can can burst down Wild & Dark Doges in 2 shots for quick hits of money, which can be helpful setting up and throughout the stage. They can also get a hit off on Gory Dark if you're lucky.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]]: With talents, C.A.T. is one of the best options there is for taking out Gory Darks very quickly, being able to take them out in 3 shots when max Talented at level 50, which normally happens within a few seconds due to the fact that C.A.T. is a rebound unit.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]: Bullet Train is a high DPH rusher with the Double Money ability that can snipe all the peons in the stage quite effectively. Similar to Can Can, the double money can help you get started early on and keep you going later on. Also acts as semi-decent chip on the bosses if you have nothing better to use it on.
*[[Li'l Tank Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Eraser Cat]]: Li'l Eraser is freeze immune, which specifically allows you to keep your ground against Deonil, who normally just freezes your meatshield lines. Gets quickly demolished by nearly everything in the stage, so don't rely on it as your only meatshield.
*[[Carpenter Cat (Rare Cat)|Rapper Cat]]: Rapper Cat is fast, wave immune, freeze immune, and resists both Deonil and the Maawths, while taking hits from the peons as well, making stalling significantly easier. If one would happen to have him at this point, which isn't too unlikely considering how easy [[Jumbo Invasion|Jumbo Jones]] is, he should be a default choice.

